  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is implicated in the regulation of Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through a shared target, Theasaponin E1, which is involved in the activation of this kinase. The evidence suggests that benzocaine acts as a target of multiple proteins, including Dual specificity testis-specific protein kinase 1 and Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1 and 3A1, all of which are targeted by Theasaponin E1. This indicates a potential mechanism where benzocaine may influence the activity of Src through the activation of Theasaponin E1, possibly by modulating the transport of substrates or signaling molecules. The consistent presence of Theasaponin E1 as a common target across different benzocaine-targeted proteins supports a role in the oncogenic pathway, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the involvement of Theasaponin E1 in the regulation of Src, suggesting a broader role in cellular processes that could be relevant to cancer progression.",
